BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Beach Metro Community News
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261128T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261128T223000
DTSTAMP:20261120T190306Z
CREATED:20261120T183325Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261120T190306Z
UID:55215-1795874400-1795905000@beachmetro.com
SUMMARY:Double Contra Dance with Jacob deGroot-Magetti\, Áine Schryer-O'Gorman & Adam Iredale-Gray
DESCRIPTION:November 28th – Double Contra Dance on the Danforth! \nWondering whether you should join us for the advanced dance? At this dance\, it is assumed that you are comfortable with all the common moves and can dance them on the fly (even if called without the caller walking the dance through beforehand). A hey should feel fun (not scary or disorienting) and it should be rare that anyone would need to help you get reoriented during a dance. If that sounds like you\, please come! \nIf you’re thinking of bringing a beginner that day\, we’d love to see them at the evening dance. Make sure they attend the intro to contra lesson at 7pm so that they have the most fun possible during the dance (and get free entry to the next regular evening dance). \n✨ On stage:\nCaller Jacob deGroot-Magetti guiding the dances\, with Áine Schryer-O’Gorman & Adam Iredale-Gray – setting the groove and keeping the floor in motion all day long. \n🕖 Evening timeline:\nAfternoon – Advanced dance (2pm to 5pm) \nEvening – Regular dance (Intro lesson 7pm\, dance 7:30 to 10:30pm) \n😷 Mask-Optional\n💧 Bring a refillable water bottle\n🥟 Samosas will be ready (arrive early if you want one!) \nAfternoon & Evening dances are priced separately.\nSliding scale: $10–$35 (kids 16 & under free)\nIt costs about $22 per dancer to make these nights happen—your support\, generosity\, and word-of-mouth keep the community strong. \n📍 St. Barnabas Church Hall\n175 Hampton Ave (near Chester Station)\n🌐 www.tcdance.org \nWhether it’s your first dance or your fiftieth\, we’d love to see you there. ❤️\n#ContraDance #Toronto #SocialDance #Community
URL:https://beachmetro.com/event/double-contra-dance-with-jacob-degroot-magetti-aine-schryer-ogorman-adam-iredale-gray/
LOCATION:St. Barnabas Church Hall\, 175 Hampton Ave\, Toronto\, M4K 2Z3
ORGANIZER;CN="Toronto Contra Dance":MAILTO:president@tcdance.org
END:VEVENT
